  "description": "SAFHOZ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H142 Ce4 Co4 O47 P12,5(C2 H3 N1),0.5(C1 H2 Cl2). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 0 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 5 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.674-3.737 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 101.14-111.03°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce4(LOEt)4(O)(O2)4(OH)2] (C68H142Ce4Co4O47P12). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
